From fa6bc17f9b6dd922e4dd5a2fc79353ba8654f150 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:27:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): fail closed on missing local repair history and
 proxy protocol errors [daveey]

A locally present original is not authority to release an assignment repair
when its blocked history has not arrived. Require a matching blocked event
with a string reason and preserve the existing authority/profile/model
checks. Refusal happens within completion's transaction, leaving the repair
and original unchanged. Ordinary routed local repairs remain supported.

Normalize http.client.HTTPException from urlopen (including HTTPError body
reads) to URLError so proxy and direct Board transports share the promised
refusal contract. Preserve the original exception and attempt diagnostics;
do not retry or widen authority. Extract unchanged peer_closed observation
to a topical transport sibling to keep the client below its file-size cap.

Why: assignment validation only ran the execution-authority check inside a
matching-history loop, with no no-match rejection. urllib also leaves HTTP
protocol/read failures unwrapped, unlike the direct kept-alive path.

Proof: synthetic local RED 5 failures (incorrect completion), GREEN 7 focused
cases including ordinary completion/policy drift. Real loopback HTTP proxy
RED 16 failures (raw IncompleteRead/BadStatusLine), GREEN 19 tests including
GET/POST, both deadline and global openers, truncated success/error bodies,
and complete 200/409/410 controls. Focused final regression: 8 files,
226 tests passed. scripts/check --base origin/main: all 21 checks passed.
No production task execution, unblock, repair mutation or raw BB data.
